WHAT THIS PROVES (the four bricks, measured not declared)
---------------------------------------------------------
1. Order      — every warrant carries a valid HMAC-SHA256 signature; a tampered payload
                fails (verify_live: "a signature is bound to the payload it signed").
2. Pre-exec   — the PII export is denied BEFORE execution and the upstream executor
                counter stays 0->0; the row count that left the perimeter is 0.
3. Brake      — /revoke is observed by the already-running agent on its NEXT call,
                latency measured on the live loop: 0.116 s (repo) / 0.122 s (console).
4. Receipt    — the hash chain recomputes from genesis after the whole vector
                (13 receipts on the fresh node, 14 on the console node).

Not claimed: platform, admin UI, multi-tenant issuer, stdio transport.


